course: dictionary
lesson: 11923
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word calculating is one of them. In maths it means working something out with numbers: «I'm calculating the total.» When it describes a person, it means cold and sneaky, always planning how to get what they want.
explain: How do you know which meaning to use? Read the words around it. Numbers, totals, change or area mean the sum meaning. A villain, a sly look or a secret plan means the sneaky meaning. «The calculating fox watched the hens and waited for its chance.» Here the fox is planning, not counting.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in the meaning. If "working out with numbers" fits the sentence, you have it. If it does not, try "cold and sneaky, always planning" instead.
fact: «Calculating» is the -ing form of the verb «calculate».
fact: «Calculate» means to work something out with numbers, such as «calculate the area».
fact: «Calculating» can also describe a person who is cold and sneaky, always planning to get what they want, often by tricking others.
fact: Phrases to know: «a calculating villain», «a cold, calculating look», «a calculating machine».
fact: The same word can have two meanings, so always check the context to find the right one.
exercise: «I'm calculating the total cost of the shopping.» What is calculating doing here? | *Working out a sum with numbers | Planning to trick the shopkeeper | Shouting at the till | Sleeping in the shop
exercise: «The calculating villain smiled and waited for his chance.» What does calculating mean? | Adding up the numbers on a bill | Very loud and cheerful | *Cold and sneaky, always planning | Kind and generous
exercise: «She stood calculating the area of the garden.» What is she doing? | *Working out the area with numbers | Digging a hole | Planning a trick | Looking at the flowers
test: «He gave her a cold, calculating look, as if he had a secret plan.» What does calculating mean here? | Warm and friendly | Adding up the price | Lost in thought about the weather | *Cold and sneaky, always planning
test: Which phrase describes a sneaky person, not a sum? | calculating the area | *a calculating villain | calculating the total | calculating the change
exam: «The calculating fox watched the hens and worked out exactly when to strike.» What does calculating mean in this sentence? | Feeling sleepy | *Cold and sneaky, planning a trick | Adding up the number of hens | Counting the eggs
